# TirNav Project Rules

## Coding Standards
- Always use TypeScript with strict mode
- Follow functional programming principles
- Use hooks instead of class components
- Implement proper error handling with try-catch
- Add JSDoc comments for complex functions

## File Structure
- One component per file
- Index.ts for barrel exports
- Separate styles into styles.ts
- Types in types.ts or separate types folder

## Performance
- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Implement useMemo and useCallback where needed
- Optimize FlatList with proper props
- Lazy load heavy components

## Naming Conventions
- Components: PascalCase
- Functions: camelCase starting with verb
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- Booleans: is/has/should prefix

## Code Quality
- No console.logs in production
- No inline styles
- No any type in TypeScript
- No unused imports
- Meaningful variable names